From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cody McGinnis <brainwart@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 16:22:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 04/12] phy: qcom: snps-femto-v2: gate clocks in system suspend

The HS PHY clocks are enabled from phy_init() until phy_exit(). The PHY
suspend callbacks only set auto-resume, so when the controller keeps the
PHY initialized across system suspend for remote wakeup, the clocks stay
on through system sleep.

On SC8280XP the HS PHYs of both Type-C controllers take "ref" from
RPMH_CXO_CLK, the RPMh XO clock that also votes in the sleep set. With
it prepared, the APPS XO vote never drops and the SoC cannot reach XO
shutdown (AOSD) or DDR self-refresh in s2idle. On a ThinkPad X13s these
two PHYs were the last direct users of bi_tcxo at machine_suspend.

Gate the clocks in the late suspend phase, after the controller has
suspended, and re-enable them in the early resume phase. Line state
wakeup is detected by the controller glue (dp/dm HS PHY interrupts), not
by the PHY.
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-snps-femto-v2.c | 31 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-snps-femto-v2.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-snps-femto-v2.c
index 75e21865b..3a49d0c24 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-snps-femto-v2.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-snps-femto-v2.c
@@ -226,6 +226,35 @@ static int __maybe_unused qcom_snps_hsphy_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 	return qcom_snps_hsphy_resume(hsphy);
 }
 
+/*
+ * The clocks are enabled from phy_init() until phy_exit(). When the
+ * controller stays initialized across system suspend (remote wakeup), gate
+ * them once the controller has suspended: the "ref" clock may be the RPMh
+ * CXO clock, which otherwise keeps XO on through system sleep. Line state
+ * wakeup is detected by the controller glue, not by the PHY.
+ */
+static int __maybe_unused qcom_snps_hsphy_suspend_late(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct qcom_snps_hsphy *hsphy = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	if (!hsphy->phy_initialized)
+		return 0;
+
+	clk_bulk_disable_unprepare(hsphy->num_clks, hsphy->clks);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static int __maybe_unused qcom_snps_hsphy_resume_early(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct qcom_snps_hsphy *hsphy = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	if (!hsphy->phy_initialized)
+		return 0;
+
+	return clk_bulk_prepare_enable(hsphy->num_clks, hsphy->clks);
+}
+
 static int qcom_snps_hsphy_set_mode(struct phy *phy, enum phy_mode mode,
 				    int submode)
 {
@@ -510,6 +539,8 @@ MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, qcom_snps_hsphy_of_match_table);
 static const struct dev_pm_ops qcom_snps_hsphy_pm_ops = {
 	SET_RUNTIME_PM_OPS(qcom_snps_hsphy_runtime_suspend,
 			   qcom_snps_hsphy_runtime_resume, NULL)
+	SET_LATE_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(qcom_snps_hsphy_suspend_late,
+				     qcom_snps_hsphy_resume_early)
 };
 
 static void qcom_snps_hsphy_override_param_update_val(
